From 03e08e37017bafe30168d9541824034d93039b4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaron Shahrabani <EMAIL>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] media: venus: hfi_cmds: skip the H.264 8x8 transform
 property on HFI 1.x

venc_set_properties() sets HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8
for every H.264 session, but only the HFI 4XX and 6XX packet builders
know that property. On HFI 1.x (MSM8916, firmware VIDEO.VE.1.8)
pkt_session_set_property_1x() falls through to its default -EINVAL,
venc_init_session() fails and VIDIOC_REQBUFS returns -EINVAL, so the
encoder cannot be used at all.

Return -ENOTSUPP for the property on HFI 1.x, which
venus_session_set_property() already treats as "not supported, skip it",
and leave the choice of transform to the firmware.

Fixes: bfee75f73c37 ("media: venus: venc: add support for V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_8X8_TRANSFORM control")
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 3ae0630..d45f7f5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1080,6 +1080,14 @@ static int pkt_session_set_property_1x(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *pkt,
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_CAPABILITY_SUPPORTED:
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_NAL_STREAM_FORMAT_SUPPORTED:
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_MULTI_VIEW_FORMAT:
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8:
+		/*
+		 * Only HFI 4XX and later know this property. The encoder sets it
+		 * unconditionally for H.264, and -EINVAL here tears the whole
+		 * session down, so report it as unsupported and let the firmware
+		 * pick the transform itself.
+		 */
+		return -ENOTSUPP;
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_MAX_SEQUENCE_HEADER_SIZE:
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_CODEC_SUPPORTED:
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VDEC_MULTI_VIEW_SELECT:
